# Debugging and Development Rules

## Debugging Best Practices

- Always use debugger statements for development and debugging
- Place debugger statements at key points in the code flow
- Use console.log sparingly, prefer debugger for interactive debugging
- Remove debugger statements before production builds
- Use meaningful variable names that make debugging easier

## Development Workflow

- Use debugger to step through code execution
- Set breakpoints at function entry points
- Debug async operations step by step
- Use debugger to inspect variable states
- Debug extension activation and command execution

## VSCode Extension Debugging

- Use debugger in extension development host
- Debug command registration and execution
- Debug provider functionality
- Use debugger to trace API calls
- Debug activation and deactivation events

